# BACKLOG I7: while a game is focused, the background is kept off the game's
# headroom (as WDDM shrinks the budgets of background processes first). A
# hidden app that loads 600 MB next to the game gets them in sysmem from the
# start, instead of taking the free memory the game streams into and being
# moved out for it a moment later.
cap 11000
proc 1614 kwin_wayland old
proc 1625 plasmashell old
proc 4841 steamwebhelper old chunk=16   # hidden behind the game
proc 5000 game chunk=64

hint 1625 v
hint 4841 h
act 1614 0 4
act 1625 0 4
act 4841 300 0
target 1614 280 0.75
target 1625 480 0.4
target 4841 200 0.8
at 10

mark the game starts focused and settles with ~1.5 GB free
hint 5000 f full
act 5000 0 30
step
target 5000 8000 0.75 spread=20
at 40

mark the hidden launcher loads 600 MB (a store page) while the game streams on
target 4841 800 0.8 spread=10
at 50
target 5000 8600 0.75 spread=20
at 80
expect born 4841 > 0              # its new memory went straight to sysmem...
expect moved_out 4841 <= 256      # ...about only what it had before was copied out (640 before)
expect denied 5000 == 0
expect sys 5000 == 0
